.TH RINT 3 "2026-05-10" "Substrate" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
rint, nearbyint \- round to nearest integer, ties to even
.SH LIBRARY
Math Library (libm, \-lm)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <math.h>
.PP
.BI "double rint(double " x ");"
.PP
.B #include <math.h>
.PP
.BI "double nearbyint(double " x ");"
.PP
.B #include <math.h>
.PP
.BI "float rintf(float " x ");"
.PP
.B #include <math.h>
.PP
.BI "float nearbyintf(float " x ");"
.PP
.B #include <math.h>
.PP
.BI "long double rintl(long double " x ");"
.PP
.B #include <math.h>
.PP
.BI "long double nearbyintl(long double " x ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.BR rint ()
and
.BR nearbyint ()
functions round
.I x
to the nearest integral value.
When the fractional part is exactly 0.5, ties are resolved by rounding to
the nearest even integer (also known as "banker's rounding").
.PP
The
.BR rintf ()
,
.BR nearbyintf ()
,
.BR rintl ()
, and
.BR nearbyintl ()
functions are float and long double variants, respectively.
.PP
The
.BR nearbyint ()
function is guaranteed not to raise the
.BR FE_INEXACT
floating-point exception.
.SH RETURN VALUE
The
.BR rint ()
and
.BR nearbyint ()
functions return the rounded integral value.
.br
If the result cannot be represented, the return value is unspecified.
.SH ERRORS
No errors are defined.
The functions do not set
.IR errno .
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
printf("\\%f\\n", rint(0.5));   /* prints 0.0 (ties to even) */
printf("\\%f\\n", rint(1.5));   /* prints 2.0 (ties to even) */
printf("\\%f\\n", rint(2.5));   /* prints 2.0 (ties to even) */
printf("\\%f\\n", rint(3.5));   /* prints 4.0 (ties to even) */
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ceil (3),
.BR floor (3),
.BR trunc (3),
.BR round (3),
.BR roundeven (3)
